      "id": "SKP-001",
      "concern": "Circuit breaker migration is not fully idempotent and risks overwriting active state with stale legacy data.",
      "severity": "CRITICAL",
      "severity_score": 850,
      "why_matters": "If a process crashes after creating the new circuit breaker files but before unlinking the legacy file, the next process will re-run the migration. This will overwrite the newly created (and potentially actively updated) files with the stale legacy state, causing lost circuit breaker events and potential routing failures.",
      "location": "§5.3 _migrate_legacy_state_if_present",
      "recommendation": "Check for the existence of the target new files (e.g., `circuit-breaker-{provider}-http_api.json`) BEFORE reading the legacy file. If the new files already exist, assume migration is complete or was interrupted, and do not overwrite them.",
      "source": "tertiary_skeptic"
    },
    {
      "id": "SKP-005",
      "concern": "Concurrency configuration fields are introduced without complete schema, loader, or validation design. headless_concurrency_scope appears in §5.6/§3.6, and headless_concurrency_limit appears in §5.6/§8, but neither is included in the advisor-strategy dataclass, model-config schema validation, or drift-gate requirements.",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "severity_score": 735,
      "why_matters": "The semaphore may be impossible to configure reliably, silently use unsafe defaults, or accept invalid values. This undermines the mandatory concurrency control path.",
      "location": "§3.1 advisor-strategy schema, §3.2 model-config validation, §3.6 migration table, §5.6 semaphore design",
      "recommendation": "Add headless_concurrency_scope to the advisor-strategy schema/dataclass with enum validation, add headless_concurrency_limit to model-config schema with integer bounds, and extend drift-gate tests to validate both fields.",
      "source": "tertiary_skeptic"
    },
    {
      "id": "SKP-004",
      "concern": "Doctor fallback probe relies solely on exit code, risking false positives for unauthenticated CLIs.",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "severity_score": 720,
      "why_matters": "Many CLIs return exit code 0 even when they fail to dispatch, instead printing interactive login prompts or 'Please log in' to stdout. Treating ANY successful response (exit 0) as auth proof will falsely mark broken CLIs as ready, leading to production dispatch failures during rollout.",
      "location": "§5.4 probe_cli_via_dispatch",
      "recommendation": "The fallback probe must inspect the stdout/stderr content for known authentication error signatures (e.g., 'login', 'unauthorized', 'session expired') rather than relying exclusively on the process return code.",
      "source": "tertiary_skeptic"
    },
    {
      "id": "SKP-002",
      "concern": "Legacy MODELINV entries do not contain dispatch_group or auth_type_resolved, but auto-mode now depends on dispatch_group-keyed history; the SDD only defaults missing auth_type to http_api and does not specify how old final_model_id values are mapped to dispatch_group.",
      "severity": "CRITICAL",
      "severity_score": 860,
      "why_matters": "The 7-day measurement window and auto-mode band comparison may silently ignore pre-cycle-110 history or misbucket it, causing cold-start defaults, biased headless selection, and invalid G-4 acceptance conclusions.",
      "location": "§3.2 dispatch_group semantics, §3.4 MODELINV v1.4 backward compatibility, §5.2 auto-mode reader",
      "recommendation": "Define a legacy-hydration rule: for each legacy MODELINV record, derive dispatch_group from current model-config using provider/final_model_id, default missing auth_type_resolved to http_api, and emit a marker for unmappable records. Add tests covering v1.3 logs participating in dispatch_group aggregation.",
      "source": "tertiary_skeptic"
    },
    {
      "id": "SKP-006",
      "concern": "N-slot semaphore acquisition can unnecessarily block or timeout while free slots exist because waiters block only on slot-0 after scanning all busy slots; if another slot releases first, the waiter will not acquire it.",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "severity_score": 705,
      "why_matters": "Under load, this can produce artificial dispatch failures, poor throughput, and misleading timeout-based circuit-breaker failures even though capacity is available.",
      "location": "§5.6 N-slot semaphore design",
      "recommendation": "Use a retry loop that periodically rescans all slots until deadline, or use a directory/lease-based counting semaphore with fair polling. Add a test where slot-1 releases before slot-0 and assert a waiter acquires promptly.",
      "source": "tertiary_skeptic"
    },
    {
      "id": "SKP-003",
      "concern": "Redaction guarantees are not consistently implemented: §1.9.1 mandates bounded streaming capture, but §5.4 doctor pseudocode uses proc.communicate() with stdout/stderr pipes, which buffers all output before redaction.",
      "severity": "CRITICAL",
      "severity_score": 845,
      "why_matters": "A malicious or malfunctioning CLI can emit large stderr/stdout containing credentials, causing memory pressure and creating raw-token residency before fail-closed redaction. This directly weakens the security fix claimed for prior blocker findings.",
      "location": "§1.9.1 Fail-closed redaction pipeline, §5.4 loa substrate doctor CLI contract",
      "recommendation": "Replace all subprocess examples and contracts with a single mandatory helper such as capture_with_byte_cap_and_redact(). Ban communicate() on captured pipes for doctor and dispatch paths unless output is redirected through the bounded streaming redactor wrapper.",
      "source": "tertiary_skeptic"
    },
    {
      "id": "SKP-001",
      "concern": "Resolver ownership is still internally inconsistent: §5.1 says the resolver no longer requires model_id and expands candidates itself, but §5.2 pseudocode still requires model_id, calls _lookup_dispatch_group(provider, model_id), and the caching contract remains keyed by model_id rather than dispatch_group.",
      "severity": "CRITICAL",
      "severity_score": 910,
      "why_matters": "This preserves the circular dependency the v1.2 change claims to remove. Implementers can build either the old model-id-driven resolver or the new candidate-expanding resolver, producing incompatible behavior and likely broken auto-mode selection.",
      "location": "§5.1 AdvisorStrategyConfig.resolve(), §5.2 auto-mode deterministic algorithm",
