    {
      "id": "SKP-002",
      "concern": "Tie-breaker cascade in auto-mode guarantees headless will almost never be selected over http_api.",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "severity_score": 780,
      "why_matters": "The tie-breaker evaluates `-seven_day_buckets[at][\"p95_ms\"]` before the `headless_preference`. Because headless CLI invocations (subprocess spawning) inherently have higher latency than direct HTTP API calls, `http_api` will consistently win the p95_ms tie-breaker when success rates are equal, completely defeating the headless-first objective.",
      "location": "§5.2 _resolve_auto (Selection cascade)",
      "recommendation": "Swap the tie-breaker order to evaluate `headless_preference` BEFORE `p95_ms`, or introduce a latency tolerance band (e.g., treat p95_ms values within 500ms of each other as equivalent) before falling back to exact latency.",
