      "concern": "Unhandled ProcessLookupError in subprocess timeout cleanup.",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "severity_score": 750,
      "why_matters": "In `probe_cli`, `os.killpg(os.getpgid(proc.pid), signal.SIGKILL)` is called on timeout. If the subprocess exits exactly as the timeout expires, the process group may no longer exist, throwing a `ProcessLookupError`. This will crash the doctor probe or the dispatch adapter entirely.",
      "location": "§5.4 probe_cli",
